<title>USA: Kansas City Southern bids for Mexican rail line.</title>
<headline>Kansas City Southern bids for Mexican rail line.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>A second-tier railroad, Kansas City Southern Industries Inc, has emerged as a key player in U.S.-Mexico trade, with a stunning $1.4 billion bid late last week for Mexico's busiest rail line, The Wall Street Journal reported Monday.</p>
<p>The bid poses risks for both Kansas City Southern and for the growing trade between the two countries because analysts say the railroad may not be big enough to handle the job and boost traffic, the story says.</p>
</text>
